  "id": "DrugBank_DB00407 - MONDO_809",
  "verbalization": "Ardeparin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Purpura Fulminans through its association with Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC), a condition characterized by widespread microthrombi and bleeding. This connection is supported by multiple pathways, all of which indicate that Ardeparin is used in the treatment or management of DIC, which in turn is linked to Purpura Fulminans. The evidence suggests that Ardeparin may exert a role in the development of DIC, potentially through mechanisms that promote clot formation or impair fibrinolysis, thereby contributing to the systemic coagulopathy seen in Purpura Fulminans. The overlapping indications across different heparin derivatives, such as Dalteparin and Heparin, further reinforce the notion that Ardeparin's involvement in DIC is a shared pathway, even though the specific mechanism remains somewhat unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of DIC as a central mediator in the relationship between Ardeparin and Purpura Fulminans.",
